  "question": "Basic Instagram-Like Platform\n\n 1) Background / Context\nThe project involves the development of a simplified version of a photo and video sharing social networking service, inspired by Instagram. The system focuses on core functionalities such as user registration, sharing photos, and interacting with shared content.\n\n 2) Objectives\n- To create a platform where users can register, upload and share photos.\n- Enable user interaction through comments and likes on photos.\n- Facilitate user connectivity by allowing users to follow one another.\n- Implement a simple tagging system for photos.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- End Users: Individuals who register to share and interact with photos.\n- Administrators: Personnel responsible for managing the system, ensuring smooth operation and maintenance.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- User Registration: Users can create an account with a unique username.\n- Photo Uploading and Sharing: Users can upload photos and share them publicly.\n- Comments: Users can comment on photos. Each comment is associated with both the user and the photo.\n- Likes: Users can like photos. A like is associated with both the user who likes it and the photo being liked.\n- Following: Users can follow other users to receive updates on their activity.\n- Tags: Photos can be tagged with keywords; users can add and manage tags on their photos.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Performance: The system should efficiently handle operations related to user interactions and photo management.\n- Scalability: Designed to support a growing number of users and interactions with minimal performance degradation.\n- Security: Ensure user data and content are stored securely, with proper authentication mechanisms for accessing accounts.\n- Usability: The interface should be intuitive and easy to navigate for a seamless user experience.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0156\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password_hash` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_users_username` (`username`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_users_email` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `photos` (\n  `photo_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `image_url` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `caption` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `is_public` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`photo_id`),\n  KEY `idx_photos_user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `photos_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `comments` (\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `photo_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment_text` varchar(1000) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_id`),\n  KEY `idx_comments_photo_id` (`photo_id`),\n  KEY `idx_comments_user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`photo_id`) REFERENCES `photos` (`photo_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `likes` (\n  `like_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `photo_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`like_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_likes_photo_user` (`photo_id`,`user_id`),\n  KEY `idx_likes_user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `likes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`photo_id`) REFERENCES `photos` (`photo_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `likes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `follows` (\n  `follower_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `followed_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`follower_user_id`,`followed_user_id`),\n  KEY `idx_follows_followed_user_id` (`followed_user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `follows_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`follower_user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `follows_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`followed_user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tags` (\n  `tag_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `tag_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`tag_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_tags_tag_name` (`tag_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `photo_tags` (\n  `photo_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `tag_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`photo_id`,`tag_id`),\n  KEY `idx_photo_tags_tag_id` (`tag_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `photo_tags_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`photo_id`) REFERENCES `photos` (`photo_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `photo_tags_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`tag_id`) REFERENCES `tags` (`tag_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
